 ## Overview
-MultiPlaneNeRF is a radiance field representation that replaces the trainable implicit encoding of vanilla NeRF with a non-trainable 2D image-based representation [S1]. It solves the problems of long training times and poor generalization to unseen data by projecting 3D points onto a set of 2D images to form an aggregate feature vector, which is then decoded by a small, shallow implicit network [S1]. Unlike vanilla NeRF, which requires separate training for each object and encodes geometry in weights, MultiPlaneNeRF allows a single decoder to generalize across many objects by simply swapping the input 2D image planes [S1].
+MultiPlaneNeRF is a radiance field representation that replaces the trainable implicit encoding of vanilla NeRF with a non-trainable 2D image-based representation [S1]. It solves the problems of long training times and poor generalization to unseen data by projecting 3D points onto a fixed set of 2D training images to create an aggregate feature vector, which is then processed by a small, generalizable implicit decoder [S1]. Unlike vanilla NeRF, which encodes object-specific geometry and color in network weights, MultiPlaneNeRF allows the representation to be swapped for new objects without retraining the decoder [S1].
 
 ## How it works
